1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:00,990
Here's a word you'll

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:02,440
see in business news.

3
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:03,320
Opaque.

4
00:00:03,320 --> 00:00:04,600
oh-PAYK.

5
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:06,590
Stress on the second syllable.

6
00:00:06,590 --> 00:00:09,320
Opaque means you can't see through it:

7
00:00:09,320 --> 00:00:10,760
hard to understand.

8
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:11,550
For example,

9
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:15,560
"The company's finances remain opaque to investors."

10
00:00:15,560 --> 00:00:17,800
The opposite is transparent.

11
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:18,510
At work,

12
00:00:18,510 --> 00:00:19,430
try:

13
00:00:19,430 --> 00:00:21,210
"This process is a little opaque."

14
00:00:21,210 --> 00:00:24,750
Try this word in your next email.

15
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:25,990
Follow The Fluent Edge

16
